# libmcrypt matches class 29 TOO -- autoreconf aborts and says so. But class 10 names the
# CAUSE (the aux file autoreconf could not find) where class 29 names only the messenger,
# so class 10 must keep it. This is the single most important negative in the file: get
# the order wrong and 31 re-files libmcrypt under a fix that does not apply to it.
AUTOTOOLS_AUX_FILE = fx("libmcrypt", """configure.in:28: installing '$with_auxdir/compile'
automake: warning: autoconf input should be named 'configure.ac', not 'configure.in'
configure.in:33: error: required file '$with_auxdir/ltmain.sh' not found
